#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *Trap 1 (Baltic Republics and CIS):* Assuming all 15 former Soviet republics joined the CIS. The three Baltic states (*Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania*) NEVER joined the CIS; they joined NATO and the EU in 2004.
  2. *Trap 2 (First Secessionist Republic):* Believing Russia or Ukraine broke away first. *Lithuania* was the first Soviet republic to declare independence in March 1990.
  3. *Trap 3 (Shock Therapy Ownership):* Believing citizens became rich stockholders through privatization vouchers. Citizens sold vouchers on the black market due to poverty; assets were cornered by criminal oligarchs.
  4. *Trap 4 (UN Security Council Seat):* Assuming the UN seat was rotated among CIS members. *Russia alone* inherited the USSR's permanent veto-bearing seat.
  5. *Trap 5 (Czechoslovakia vs Yugoslavia Disintegration):* Inverting the conflict patterns. Czechoslovakia split completely peacefully (*Velvet Divorce*); Yugoslavia disintegrated in genocidal ethnic warfare.
  6. *Trap 6 (Nature of Shock Therapy):* Assuming Shock Therapy was a gradual, state-guided reform like China's Open Door Policy. Shock Therapy was an abrupt, instantaneous, unregulated transition to capitalism.
  7. *Trap 7 (Gorbachev's Intention):* Believing Gorbachev wanted to destroy the USSR. He intended to reform and revitalize socialism; the collapse was an unintended consequence of democratization and nationalist awakenings.
]

